course: dictionary
lesson: 3258
title: Equality: the same chance for everyone
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Equality means being equal. When people have the same rights, chances and respect, there is equality between them, whatever their sex, skin colour, religion, disability or background. «Equality means nobody hits anybody, not that everybody may hit everybody.» The same rule applies to everyone, and nobody gets to break it.
explain: Equality can also be a maths word. Two amounts that are the same are equal, and a statement with an equals sign, like 3 + 4 = 7, is an equality: both sides balance. Look at the words around equality to see which meaning the writer means.
explain: Equality and equity sound alike, but they are not the same. «Equality gives everyone the same; equity gives each person what they need to have the same chance.» Equity can mean giving extra help to those who need it, so fair treatment can look different for different people.
explain: Be careful when a big word is used to excuse bad behaviour. Connor says he is «all for equality», but later he says «I hit her because equality». That does not make sense, because equality means nobody hits anybody. Ask yourself: does what I am doing treat everyone with respect?
fact: Equality means everyone has the same rights, chances and respect.
fact: In maths, equality means two amounts are the same, like 3 + 4 = 7.
fact: Equity means giving each person what they need to have the same chance.
fact: The Quakers, the Religious Society of Friends, are known for peace-making and equality.
fact: Phrases to know: equality of opportunity, gender equality, racial equality, fight for equality.
exercise: «Equality means nobody hits anybody, not that everybody may hit everybody.» What does equality mean in this sentence? | Being very loud | Everyone may hit everyone | Only some people may hit others | *The same rules and respect for everyone
exercise: In maths, 3 + 4 = 7 is an example of what? | A picture | A type of sport | A fight | *An equality
exercise: What does «equality of opportunity» mean? | Only the strongest get a chance | Opportunity is only for rich people | Nobody has any chance | *Everyone has the same chance
test: Which word means giving each person what they need to have the same chance? | Equality | *Equity | Equalizer | Equator
test: Connor says «I hit her because equality». Why is his excuse wrong? | Hitting is part of equality because everyone is the same | Equality is the reason to hit people | *Equality means nobody hits anybody, so hitting goes against it | Equality only applies to maths
exam: «Quakers are known for peace-making and equality.» What does this tell you about Quakers? | They are known for shouting | *They value peace and fair treatment for everyone | They only meet in winter | They dislike all people
